---
name: "IOQ Protocol (Showcase)"
description: "Every feature in one template: match/case scenarios, if/elif, methods, slicing, typed inputs, built-ins, inline expressions, LaTeX markup with TOC, tables, labels and figures"
markup: latex
variables:
  client: ""
  equipment: ""
  equipment_count: ""
  qualification_date: ""
  review_time: ""
  gmp_critical: ""
  author: ""
types:
  equipment_count: number
  qualification_date: date
  review_time: time
  gmp_critical: yesno
docx:
  font: "Calibri"
  size: 11
  header: "IOQ Protocol — controlled document"
---
#SCRIPT
# ---- scenario: client profile (appears as a dropdown when generating a child) ----
match client:
    case "ABC Corp":
        company_name = "ABC Corporation Inc."
        company_code = "ABC"
        approver = "Tan Wei Ming"
    case "XYZ Ltd":
        company_name = "XYZ Limited"
        company_code = "XYZ"
        approver = "Nur Aisyah"
    case _:
        company_name = client
        company_code = client[:3].upper()
        approver = "TBD"

# ---- derived values: methods, slicing, ternary, membership ----
title = "IOQ — " + equipment.strip()
header_tag = company_code + "-" + equipment.strip()[:8].upper().replace(" ", "-")
criticality = "GMP-critical" if gmp_critical == "yes" else "non-critical"
lab_note = "on-site" if "Lab" in equipment else "standard"

# ---- typed inputs: number / date / time (guarded while still empty) ----
if equipment_count != "":
    units = float(equipment_count)
    effort_label = format(units * 1.5, "0.0") + " day(s)"
else:
    effort_label = "TBD"

if qualification_date != "" and review_time != "":
    schedule_line = "scheduled " + qualification_date + " at " + review_time
elif qualification_date != "":
    schedule_line = "scheduled " + qualification_date
else:
    schedule_line = "to be scheduled"

# ---- built-ins ----
generated_on = str(system.date) + " " + str(system.time)
signature = author.strip() + " / " + system.username
#ENDSCRIPT
\begin{center}
\textbf{ {header_tag}: {title} }
Prepared for {company_name} — issued \today
\end{center}
\hrule

\tableofcontents
% the TOC above lists every numbered section; in Word, press F9 to add page numbers

\section{Overview} \label{sec:overview}
Prepared for \textbf{ {company_name} } — {criticality} qualification, {lab_note} handling.\\
Document \texttt{ {doc.name} }, from template \texttt{ {doc.template} }, generated {generated_on}.

\subsection{Scope}
This protocol qualifies {= equipment.strip() }: installation checks, operational checks,
and acceptance criteria. Estimated effort: \underline{ {effort_label} }, {schedule_line}.
Approval flow is defined in section \ref{sec:approval}; \emph{execution} in section \ref{sec:execution}.

\subsection{Roles}
\begin{description}
\item[Approver] {approver} — reviews \& signs the executed protocol
\item[Author] {signature}
\item[Units under test] {equipment_count}
\end{description}

\section{Execution} \label{sec:execution}
\subsection{Installation checks}
\begin{tabular}{lcr}
Step & Check & Units \\
\hline
1 & Delivery matches PO {= "PO-" + company_code + "-" + str(system.year) } & {equipment_count} \\
2 & Environment (temperature, power, clearance) & {equipment_count} \\
3 & Utilities connected \& labelled & {equipment_count} \\
\end{tabular}

\subsection{Operational checks}
\begin{enumerate}
\item Execute operational runs and record results
\item Confirm alarms \textit{(power loss, sensor fault)}
\item Record deviations, if any
\end{enumerate}

\subsubsection{Acceptance criteria}
\begin{quote}
Approved when 100\% of checks pass and all deviations are closed.
\end{quote}

\section{Approval} \label{sec:approval}
Literal braces stay literal when doubled: {{not_a_variable}}.

\begin{verbatim}
raw block: markup like \textbf{...} is kept exactly as typed here
\end{verbatim}

\newpage
\section*{Appendix (unnumbered)}
Refer back to \ref{sec:overview} for scope. Signature: ________________  Date: {system.date}